From c2b465a9a53441e02be90438302ce98e0ba1e75c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:06:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 114/123] gui: stop a directory backup in the middle of a
 folder on cancel

The Stop button was only honoured between two folders: the PXAR walk
ignored the cancel, so a backup of one large folder ran to its end.

PXARArchive gets a Cancelled hook, checked before every 64 KiB block it
writes; once it fires the walk returns ErrWriteCancelled. backupReal sets
it from the run's context, checks again before closing the indexes, and
the chunk upload retries now derive from that context. The directory
loop then drops the session instead of finishing it, so nothing of the
interrupted folder is committed, and reports the run as cancelled.

Reported in rdemsystems/NimbusBackupClient#12.
